.TH COASTLINE-IMPORT 1 "@COASTLINE_MAN_DATE@" "Coastline @CMAKE_PROJECT_VERSION@" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
coastline-import \- convert game disc and ROM assets for Coastline
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B coastline
.RI [ options ]
.B import \-\-cd
.I DISC
.B \-\-rom
.I ROM
.RI [ "\-\-rom ROM" ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Import a Boss Rally disc image or mounted disc directory with at least one
supported Top Gear Rally ROM.
Both the disc and a ROM are required.
ROM images are identified by SHA-1 after normalising their byte order.
USA, European, and Japanese releases can be imported in one batch.
.PP
Conversion produces PNG images, FLAC audio, glTF models, and JSON metadata.
Successful imports replace generated packs and preserve custom mod packs.
Original game files must be supplied by the user.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-cd " DISC"
Read a Boss Rally CUE sheet, ISO, Mode 1 BIN, numbered track file, CloneCD,
DiscJuggler CDI, Alcohol MDS, or Nero NRG image.
A directory can be the root of a mounted physical disc or a copy of its files.
Directory sources import data without CD audio.
A BIN image uses a matching adjacent CUE sheet when available.
Without a CUE sheet, known whole-file SHA-1 digests select verified track offsets.
Other BIN images use sector headers and audio pregaps to discover a layout.
Uncertain layouts and ISO images import data without CD audio.
Numbered Track NN.bin sets, CloneCD .ccd/.img, DiscJuggler .cdi,
Alcohol .mds/.mdf, and Nero .nrg files
also provide audio tracks.
MDS supports split files and UTF-16 filenames.
NRG supports disc-at-once and track-at-once metadata with 32-bit or 64-bit offsets.
CDI supports versions 2, 3, and 3.5, multiple sessions, and stored pregaps.
P-Q and P-W subchannel bytes are discarded during conversion.
Track files referenced by a CUE sheet must remain available.
.TP
.BI \-\-rom " ROM"
Read a Top Gear Rally ROM image.
Repeat for each release to include.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print subcommand usage and exit.
.PP
Global options precede import.
Use \-\-data-dir to select the destination.
An explicit data directory imports without creating normal configuration or
log files.
.SH FILES
Generated assets are written below assets/default in the data directory.
Other generated regional and Pure PC packs are written beside default.
Without \-\-data-dir, adjacent portable assets take precedence when present and
portable lookup is enabled; otherwise the platform user data directory is used.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
coastline import \-\-cd "Boss Rally.cue" \-\-rom usa.z64
coastline \-\-data-dir ./game-data import \-\-cd rally.iso \e
  \-\-rom usa.z64 \-\-rom jpn.z64
.fi
.SH EXIT STATUS
Zero indicates a successful import.
A nonzero status indicates invalid arguments, unsupported input, or conversion
failure.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR coastline (1),
.BR coastline-import-pak (1),
.BR coastline-run-script (1)
